{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f12-fa6f-76e2-8836-346b2c16c0e2"},"sequence":280,"recorded_at":1780531400000555,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"1d2caafb-0af4-4757-b512-da8d26434a41"},"task_id":"1d2caafb-0af4-4757-b512-da8d26434a41","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"1d2caafb-0af4-4757-b512-da8d26434a41","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/worktree/internal/provhost/doc.go`.\n1|// Package provhost implements the ax host side of the provider plugin\n2|// JSON-over-stdio protocol of pinned specification Section 7.2: one-frame\n3|// JSONL transport, deadlines, size limits, stdout/stderr separation,\n4|// operation dispatch, and status recovery.\n5|//\n6|// The actor every Section 7.2 RFC 2119 keyword governs here is the ax host\n7|// (this repository). The provider plugin is a child process this package\n8|// starts but never trusts: every byte it emits is attacker-influenced, so\n9|// every frame is validated before any member is used, and a different-major\n10|// payload is never parsed far enough to trust its error code, retryable\n11|// bit, details, or authority fields (Section 15.1).\n12|//\n13|// This package owns the envelope layer only. Operation dispatch means the\n14|// host maps an operation name to one plugin invocation and refuses unknown\n15|// names locally without spawning: the exact request and success body shapes\n16|// of Section 7.5, the manifest/probe/capability vocabularies of Sections\n17|// 7.3-7.4, profile mapping (7.7), quiescence semantics (7.6), and mutation\n18|// idempotency receipts are owned by the conformance leaf of this story, not\n19|// here. Request and success bodies cross this package opaquely except for\n20|// two structural checks the framing layer needs: a body must be a JSON\n21|// object, and the materialize-status body this package interprets for\n22|// recovery must satisfy the state/nullability/identity rules Section 7.5\n23|// states for ProviderTransactionStatus.\n24|//\n25|// A failed read is never an absence: a crashed, timed-out, oversized,\n26|// unparsable, or correlation-mismatched invocation fails with a local\n27|// Structured Error 1.0.0, never with a partial response the caller could\n28|// mistake for a result. Status recovery is fail-closed the same way: an\n29|// unknown or integrity-invalid transaction fails with integrity_failure\n30|// and must be quarantined rather than represented as a successful status.\n31|//\n32|// The package mutates no durable state of its own and keeps no cross-call\n33|// cache: Host starts one plugin process per operation, so successive calls\n34|// are separate processes observing durable state through the authority the\n35|// caller passes, which is the property the cross-process recovery cases\n36|// rest on. Retry decisions belong to the caller; every local failure this\n37|// package emits is non-retryable, because nothing observed at an unusable\n38|// frame licenses a safe-retry claim.\n39|//\n40|// Stated bounds: stderr capture is capped at 1 MiB (an implementation\n41|// resource bound, not a protocol limit); error details carry the failure\n42|// class, member names, and the observed version string only — never\n43|// environment or stderr content. Mutation idempotency ((operation,\n44|// operation_id) receipts, byte-identical replay, idempotency_mismatch)\n45|// is not implemented here.\n46|package provhost"}}}
