{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6b3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f12-fa6f-76e2-8836-346b2c16c0e2"},"sequence":436,"recorded_at":1780531400000867,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"e1f2b6ce-7e29-4238-a14e-8fe10ebd1a37"},"task_id":"e1f2b6ce-7e29-4238-a14e-8fe10ebd1a37","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"e1f2b6ce-7e29-4238-a14e-8fe10ebd1a37","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-1zvmw7/TASK-260830-1zvmw7_rework-evidence.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1zvmw7 — Round-1 rework evidence (rev2)\n2|\n3|Base: leaf-1 checkpoint `9481a20` + uncommitted round-1 CR candidate.\n4|Working tree only — nothing committed, per the Change Request shape.\n5|\n6|## Production changes (`internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go`)\n7|\n8|- F1: `CheckOperation` admits `manifest`/`probe` for any admitted set\n9|  (empty included) — §4.D gives both `Capability dependencies: none`.\n10|  Doc comment reconciled with `CapabilitiesForOperation`.\n11|- F8: removed the dead `checkProbeIdentity` inner branch (backend IDs are\n12|  already equal where it stood — substitution is always untrusted now),\n13|  removed the `parsePlatformList` duplicate check subsumed by `>=`,\n14|  corrected the `checkEvidenceSet` doc (whole-reconciliation refusal).\n15|\n16|## Test changes\n17|\n18|- Structural root: every refusal assertion in `manifest_test.go` and\n19|  `manifest_pin_test.go` now names `*Error.Detail` via\n20|  `requireRefusal`/`requirePinRefusal` (was 0/29).\n21|- F2: narrowed 4 fixtures until only the named rule rejects —\n22|  omission/static-echo withdraw the orphaned evidence, protocol moves the\n23|  evidence with the probe, false-claim lists the new evidence ID.\n24|  `dangling evidence id` flips the withdrawn claim false so it reaches\n25|  the ID-set arm (a bare deletion lands on coverage first).\n26|- F3: substitution fixture tracks the foreign digest in the probe, so only\n27|  the manifest↔record gate can refuse.\n28|- F4: `evidence expires at admission instant` row (`expires_at == now`).\n29|- F5: `ParseProbe`/`ParseEvidence` gain schema/schema_version/\n30|  backend-identity/kind/digest cases; all three parsers gain an\n31|  `unknown implementation kind` case.\n32|- F6: adjacent-duplicate cases (sorted position, holds the `>=` halves),\n33|  `unprefixed valid base64 signature`, `null realm members on realm claim`.\n34|- F7: `claim list bound` (17), `evidence list bound` (257),\n35|  `empty platforms`, `overlong os version` (257).\n36|- G-A: `TestParsedClaimSlicesShareNoRegistryBacking` (white-box) poisons\n37|  every parsed claim slice and re-reads the interior.\n38|- F1: `TestCheckOperationAdmitsDependencyFreeOperations`.\n39|- F9: README `15.3#3` re-scoped, `terminal-manifest-probe-admission`\n40|  acceptance case registered, projection digest re-pinned, README and\n41|  golden figures 74→75 acceptance cases.\n42|\n43|## Verification (all run directly, exit codes observed)\n44|\n45|- Targeted fix mutants: 24/24 KILLED (`/tmp/rev/verify-fixes.py`,\n46|  exit 0). Every mutant grep-confirmed present (anchor count == 1),\n47|  `go vet` clean, reverted (tree equals pre-run bytes).\n48|- Deletion-mechanism probe: all 6 narrowed fixtures fail with\n49|  `error = <nil>` under gate deletion — the gate admits what it must\n50|  reject; no lower arm catches the fixture.\n51|- Adjacent-vs-descending control: adjacent cases KILLED by M41/M60;\n52|  the old descending cases pass under the narrowed gate (caught by `>`),\n53|  proving the new cases carry the dup halves.\n54|- Reviewer battery-1 re-run: 46 KILLED / 0 SURVIVED. 12 COMPILE-FAIL are\n55|  battery-1 formulation artifacts (deleted code leaves an unused binding);\n56|  battery-2's compilable variants of all 12 are KILLED. M37/M58 anchors\n57|  changed by the F1/F8 edits — re-anchored equivalents both KILLED.\n58|- Reviewer battery-2 re-run: 43 KILLED / 4 SURVIVED, exactly the expected\n59|  remainder: M71/M72 (JCS unprovable — closed schemas use ASCII-only keys\n60|  with no numbers, so Go marshalling and RFC 8785 agree byte for byte;\n61|  reported as bound, not coverage) and M92/M95 (near-equivalents).\n62|- G-A positive control (parseClaim returns row slices): the new pin\n63|  FAILS while the full shipped suite previously passed with it live.\n64|- Full suite: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0, 14/14 packages ok\n65|  (`/tmp/rev/full-suite.log`). Package coverage 88.6% (was 87.1%).\n66|  `go vet ./...` exit 0. `gofmt -l .` empty.\n67|- Traceability: `internal/traceability` + `cmd/tracecheck` green;\n68|  projection digest re-pinned to\n69|  `892bdb6a…bf806a035`; section coverage unchanged\n70|  (49 bindings, 17/403 clauses).\n71|\n72|## Stated bounds inherited\n73|\n74|JCS canonicalization unprovable with these fixtures (M71/M72 survive as a\n75|property of the fixtures, not a defect). M92/M95 near-equivalent. No new\n76|bounds introduced."}}}
