{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c82f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f12-fa6f-76e2-8836-346b2c16c0e2"},"sequence":626,"recorded_at":1780531400001247,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"15b1320d-120d-48dd-aa9b-1436d50ecf30"},"task_id":"15b1320d-120d-48dd-aa9b-1436d50ecf30","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"15b1320d-120d-48dd-aa9b-1436d50ecf30","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-21-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '381,420p' README.md; echo \\\"===LOGBOOK===\\\"; grep -n \\\"0429\\\\|narrowing\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head; wc -l LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"View discovery section and logbook claims\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"## Provider Plugin Discovery and Trust\\n\\n[`internal/provider`](internal/provider) implements the Section 7.1 trusted\\nprovider plugin host boundary: deterministic executable discovery, trust\\nrecording, and substitution detection. `Discover` is the production entry\\npoint. It enumerates candidates in the section's source order — configured\\n`providers.plugin_dirs` in listed order (entry names sorted bytewise within\\neach directory), then the six built-in adapters (`codex`, `claude`, `gemini`,\\n`muse`, `antigravity`, `pi`), then `PATH` only when `allow_path_plugins` is\\ntrue — and records the canonical absolute path, SHA-256 digest, and approving\\nowner for every accepted external `ax-provider-<id>` executable. Symlinks are\\nresolved before comparison, the target must be a regular file owned by the\\noperator or an administrator-approved identity, and `Trust`/`Verify` carry the\\nreceipt a changed path target or digest must renew.\\n\\nIf two candidates declare the same provider ID, discovery fails with\\n`invalid_config` before either is probed or executed; the package has no probe\\nor execution dependency, and no source imports a process-execution facility, so\\nthe ordering holds structurally. Filesystem read failures abort discovery with\\n`local_precondition_failed` instead of yielding a partial set, and a receipt\\nthat no longer matches freshly read facts fails verification with\\n`integrity_failure`. All three codes are pinned against the contract registry\\nwith their exact exits (3, 3, 9). A discovered candidate carries no\\navailability, status, or capability claim, and the package is an internal M0\\nhost boundary, not a public stable plugin SDK, which the section defers. The\\npackage mutates no durable state: the host persists the `TrustRecord`, and\\n`Verify` rechecks it. Native Windows owner attestation is unimplemented, so\\nexternal executables are undiscoverable there until a Windows owner model\\nlands; built-in adapters are unaffected.\\n\\nRun the focused tests and coverage with:\\n\\n```bash\\ngo test ./internal/provider -count=1\\ngo test ./internal/provider -cover -count=1\\n```\\n\\n## Provider Plugin JSONL Protocol\\n\\n[`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost) implements the ax host side of\\n===LOGBOOK===\\n8:### 0429 — Provider JSONL host leaf: protocol transport, three inherited findings, one repeated harness failure\\n17:- EVIDENCE: 25 narrowing mutants, each verified present, compiling, and restored — 25 killed, 0 survivors. `go test ./...` exit 0 (15/15), `-race` exit 0 in batches over all 15, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `gofmt` clean, `tracecheck` exit 0, catalog generate current.\\n36:- ROOT CAUSE: entry 1632's generalisation, for the third recorded time. Round 2 closed the four guards the review named and did not enumerate the rest of the path. `OwnerPolicy.Approves` is the next guard inside `trustCandidate` after the two that were fixed, and `TestDiscoverRefusesRelativePluginDir` is the single-entry twin of the multi-entry PATH fixture the same round wrote — narrowing the `plugin_dirs` absolute gate to `index == 0` also survives the full suite. The remedy for \\\"proven at one sample\\\" is the traversal, not the named fix.\\n49:- FINDING: the digest guard is proven at 1 of 32 bytes; narrowing `provider.go:466` to `sum[:1]` survives, because both fixture pairs happen to differ in their first byte. The `identity != record.owner` half of `provider.go:458` has no test at all — `adminUID = 7` is declared at `fake_test.go:118` and never used, and it is exactly the fixture that case needs.\\n75:- FINDING (reviewer observation, correction to the record): three mutants were dismissed in round 5 on the grounds that \\\"none is a registered code\\\". `terminal_backend_capability_unproven` IS registered at Structured Error 1.3.0 exit 6 (`catalog_gen.go:541`), and sparing it in `ExitCodeFor`'s version scoping survives on a clean tree. The conclusion holds for a different reason — the same narrowing on `observation_gap` is killed by `TestExitCodeForRefusesVersionAndCodeDrift`, so the class has a covered representative. The dismissal stands; the sentence behind it did not. A survivor dismissed with a wrong reason is worse than one dismissed with none, because the reason is what the next round trusts.\\n78:- EVIDENCE: harness grown from 63 to 86 mutants — 85 killed, 1 declared subsumed (unchanged), 0 unexplained survivors, 64 narrowing by the harness's own definition, suite restored green after every batch. Supersedes the \\\"63 mutants at 62 killed\\\" figure in the 1447 entry below. One mutant on the §1.6 disclosure was DISCARDED as equivalent and replaced: disabling the assertion in the test changes no outcome while the gap is open, so the replacement closes the gap in production and requires the pin to redden. Same stated bound: the harness mutates the tree, lives under `.temp/`, and no committed artifact derives its counts.\\n84:- FINDING: this was a reachable bypass and not only an unmeasured ratio. `code` and `exit_code` are two independent members of one document, and this guard is the sole thing binding them. The retryability refusal this package publishes keys on the EXIT STATUS for three whole classes — 7 authorization, 16 policy refusal, 130 interrupt — so relabelling a code out of its own class asks that refusal about the wrong class and it stays silent. Under the narrowing, `{\\\"code\\\":\\\"authentication_failed\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":9,\\\"retryable\\\":true}` was ADMITTED by `cliresult.Read` at exit status 9, and the caller received a `Reading` naming an authorization failure with `Retryable() == true`. The §14.2 exit-status corroboration cannot see it, because the process really did exit with the relabelled status.\\n92:- EVIDENCE: harness grown from 53 to 63 mutants — 62 killed, 1 declared subsumed (unchanged), 0 unexplained survivors, 44 narrowing by the harness's own definition, suite restored green. Supersedes the \\\"53 mutants at 52 killed\\\" figure in the 1421 entry below. Same stated bound: the harness mutates the tree, lives under `.temp/`, and no committed artifact derives its counts.\\n102:- FINDING (reviewer Observation A, extended and acted on rather than recorded as a bound): the reviewer measured that narrowing `axerror.requireCommonDataModel` to skip documents over 4096 bytes SURVIVES, because every duplicate-member fixture is hand-built and short, and declined to block because byte length is not a §1.6 dimension. The identical narrowing on `documentSchema`'s copy of the same gate in `cliresult` also survived — the finding was reported for one reader and holds in both. Both are closed with a conforming document several times that size: a Structured Error padded through its 64-key `details` bound, and a CLI Result carrying twelve Session Summaries.\\n103:- DECISION: give a size fixture ONE knob. The first padding helper padded through both the 4096-character `message` bound and the `details` map, so narrowing either loop alone left the document over 4096 and the mutant survived as an equivalent one. Padding through `details` alone makes the narrowed loop redden the row's own length assertion. A fixture whose size has two independent sources cannot be shown to fail closed.\\n     732 LOGBOOK.md\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7191,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1798,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
