{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c853","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f12-fa6f-76e2-8836-346b2c16c0e2"},"sequence":644,"recorded_at":1780531400001283,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3059dba8-1002-442f-83f4-b0e47671bbbf"},"task_id":"3059dba8-1002-442f-83f4-b0e47671bbbf","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3059dba8-1002-442f-83f4-b0e47671bbbf","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-22-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '1,35p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read logbook head entry 0429\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-05\\n\\n### 0429 — Provider JSONL host leaf: protocol transport, three inherited findings, one repeated harness failure\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-qcosxq (story leaf 2). New `internal/provhost` (§7.2 framing/lifecycle, §7.5 dispatch names, status recovery; bodies opaque except status rules), plus F18/F19/F20 closures in `internal/provider` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FINDING: F18 closed with the verdict's four-line pin (`ownerAttester` pointer-equals `fileOwnerUID`); SEAM1 verified red before restore. F19 closed by planting a distinct-ID candidate in each absolute dir of `TestDiscoverRefusesRelativePluginDir`; the `return out` mutant returns 1 candidate and reddens. F20 closed with a `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` CI step; a planted type error in `os_windows_test.go` verified the step sees the file.\\n- FINDING: the §7.3/§7.5 operation registry counts 15, not 16 — the manifest JSON and the §7.5 table both list manifest, probe, launch, identify-session, quiesce, native-store-plan, capture, materialize, materialize-status, materialize-commit, materialize-rollback, resume, fork, stop, doctor. The ownership gap prose saying \\\"16-entry\\\" miscounts; the registry test derives the 15 from the pinned table in order.\\n- ANOMALY: repeated entry 2113 exactly — the mutant sweep restored via `git checkout` on untracked files, silently no-opping, so mutants accumulated and every verdict after the first was taken on a red mask. Caught because later mutants stopped compiling. Recovery: byte-level reversal of every applied pair (one 2x over-replace repaired by hand), then a clean re-run with `cp` backups, per-mutant presence assertions, and restore verification.\\n- DECISION: transport lives in `internal/provhost`, not `internal/provider` — leaf 1's `TestDiscoveryReachesNoProcess` fails any `os/exec` import in the discovery package, and weakening that scan would resurrect a round-3 kill. Local failures are `*axerror.Error` via six instrumented constructors (audited bidirectionally with a closed six-code set); child failures surface through `DecodeBound` under the static provider-major-2 binding and `LocalFromUntrusted` for first-frame faults.\\n- ANOMALY: the sleep-past-deadline test exposed a real defect, not a test artifact — killing only the direct child leaves grandchildren holding the pipes, hanging the wait past the deadline. Fixed with process-group kill on unix (direct-child kill on Windows, stated) plus `WaitDelay` and stream abandonment; the test bounds elapsed time below the drain delay to pin it.\\n- BOUND: provhost cover 86.1% statements; the remainder is constructor-error propagation branches (constructors proven total by an explicit test) and `ExecRunner` stdin-failure races. Full body vocabularies and mutation idempotency receipts belong to the conformance leaf; no §7.2 clause newly discharged (`tracecheck` unchanged at 17/403, 74 cases).\\n- EVIDENCE: 25 narrowing mutants, each verified present, compiling, and restored — 25 killed, 0 survivors. `go test ./...` exit 0 (15/15), `-race` exit 0 in batches over all 15, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `gofmt` clean, `tracecheck` exit 0, catalog generate current.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0327 — The fourth enumeration failure: the refusal inventory could derive nothing and pass\\n\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provider` round-3 rework of TASK-260830-2890sd (findings F11–F17).\\n- FINDING: `auditRefusalInventory` derived its domain from package source, then asserted only that every derived site was exercised. Four mutants stayed green: empty domain, 1-of-N domain, skipping `provider.go` entirely, and a planted stray `Error{}` plus an empty-but-successful wrong-cwd read. The same stray alone reddened, which locates the hole precisely in the derivation, not the check. This is entry 0230's defect one level up, and the fourth recorded instance of \\\"closed the guards the review named, did not enumerate the rest\\\" — the package already carried the floor three times (`TestDiscoveryReachesNoProcess`, `TestCandidatesAdvertiseNoCapability`, the source inventory's exact counts) while the identical file-scan idiom in the refusal inventory had none.\\n- FIX: bidirectional inventory — `ScannedFiles` floor (\\\"scanned no production sources; the check is blind\\\"), empty-sites floor (\\\"derived no refusal sites; the scan is blind\\\"), and a reverse check requiring every exercised site to resolve to a derived site. The reverse bound is derived from the test run, not hand-listed, so truncation reddens without a magic number. Floors that must survive early-return mutants live at the caller (`TestSection71AdvertisesNoPublicSDK` for `exportedSymbols`); a floor inside the helper is bypassed by `return nil` at its top. `auditRefusalInventory` floors live in the audit itself, so they hold for the same reason.\\n- FINDING: the production `OSSystem` seam had zero negative tests — eight survivors in one file. Three are entry 0230's uid-0 twin on the attestation side (`Inspect` swallowing the error as uid 0, `fileOwnerUID` returning `0, nil` against its own doc comment, `CurrentOperatorPolicy` seeding `{0}`), one inverts the headline invariant at the only violable point (`ReadDir` error as absence). The `Inspect` attestation-error branch is unreachable with real stat results on unix, so it is forced through a documented `ownerAttester` variable — the only seam that makes the branch testable rather than merely readable.\\n- BOUND: `Geteuid`-vs-`Getuid` is environment-equivalent on any host where euid == uid (here `euid=502 uid=502`, probed); the test pins `OperatorUID` to the effective uid and kills the `{0}`-wildcard mutant, and the residual is recorded, not waved through. Native Windows refusal is covered by a build-tagged test compiled via `GOOS=windows go vet`, not executed here.\\n- EVIDENCE: 19-mutant harness over every rev4 survivor shape: 18 RED, 1 environment-equivalent green (G40b). `go test ./...` exit 0, provider cover 97.0%, `go vet`/`GOOS=windows go vet`/`GOOS=windows go build` clean.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. TASK-260830-2890sd round-3 rework, handed to review uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n\\n## 2026-09-04\\n\\n### 0230 — The guard the round did not sweep was the one that matters: uid 0 admitted, suite green\\n\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provider` round-2 review of TASK-260830-2890sd at `d8fc669`; §7.1. 32 mutants, 30 caught, 2 survived.\\n- FINDING: injecting `if uid == 0 { return true }` into `OwnerPolicy.Approves` (`provider.go:143`) leaves `go test ./... -count=1` GREEN across all 14 packages. No test in the package uses uid 0 — `fakeUID = 1000`, `foreignUID = 2000`, `adminUID = 7`. The property is asserted three times and measured zero times: the production doc comment at `provider.go:139` (\\\"no superuser exception is implied\\\"), the outcome artifact (\\\"no implied superuser\\\"), and the §7.1 MUST pinned verbatim at `enumeration_test.go:135` (\\\"owned by the operator or an administrator-approved identity\\\"). Root-owned system PATH directories are the first case a real host meets, so this is the realistic identity, not an exotic one. Confirmed by isolation: a probe driving `Discover` with a uid-0 file under an operator-only policy PASSes against intact production and FAILs under the injection.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7442,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1861,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
