he error as uid 0, `fileOwnerUID` returning `0, nil` against its own doc comment, `CurrentOperatorPolicy` seeding `{0}`), one inverts the headline invariant at the only violable point (`ReadDir` error as absence). The `Inspect` attestation-error branch is unreachable with real stat results on unix, so it is forced through a documented `ownerAttester` variable — the only seam that makes the branch testable rather than merely readable.\\n- BOUND: `Geteuid`-vs-`Getuid` is environment-equivalent on any host where euid == uid (here `euid=502 uid=502`, probed); the test pins `OperatorUID` to the effective uid and kills the `{0}`-wildcard mutant, and the residual is recorded, not waved through. Native Windows refusal is covered by a build-tagged test compiled via `GOOS=windows go vet`, not executed here.\\n- EVIDENCE: 19-mutant harness over every rev4 survivor shape: 18 RED, 1 environment-equivalent green (G40b). `go test ./...` exit 0, provider cover 97.0%, `go vet`/`GOOS=windows go vet`/`GOOS=windows go build` clean.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. TASK-260830-2890sd round-3 rework, handed to review uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n\\n## 2026-09-04\\n\\n### 0230 — The guard the round did not sweep was the one that matters: uid 0 admitted, suite green\\n\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provider` round-2 review of TASK-260830-2890sd at `d8fc669`; §7.1. 32 mutants, 30 caught, 2 survived.\\n- FINDING: injecting `if uid == 0 { return true }` into `OwnerPolicy.Approves` (`provider.go:143`) leaves `go test ./... -count=1` GREEN across all 14 packages. No test in the package uses uid 0 — `fakeUID = 1000`, `foreignUID = 2000`, `adminUID = 7`. The property is asserted three times and measured zero times: the production doc comment at `provider.go:139` (\\\"no superuser exception is implied\\\"), the outcome artifact (\\\"no implied superuser\\\"), and the §7.1 MUST pinned verbatim at `enumeration_test.go:135` (\\\"owned by the operator or an administrator-approved identity\\\"). Root-owned 