{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf5b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f12-fa6f-76e2-8836-346b2c16c0e2"},"sequence":1544,"recorded_at":1780531400003083,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"ab72a716-b933-44c5-ab2b-51fdfc188707"},"task_id":"ab72a716-b933-44c5-ab2b-51fdfc188707","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"ab72a716-b933-44c5-ab2b-51fdfc188707","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-05\n-\n-### 0429 — Provider JSONL host leaf: protocol transport, three inherited findings, one repeated harness failure\n+## 2026-09-05\n+\n+### 0435 — Provider JSONL host leaf round-2 rework: arm identity, exact bounds, production-site pins\n+\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-qcosxq round-1 verdict (changes requested, 44/66 killed, 18 real survivors). Test-only rework in `internal/provhost` plus README/LOGBOOK honesty items; production untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n+- FIX (F25, structural, first): every refusal row now names its arm — `requireFrameRefusal` (code + `member` detail + rule detail + non-retryable) for frame refusals, `requireLocalRefusal` (code + rule detail + non-retryable) for invalid_config/integrity/timeout/process arms, plus `observed`-version assertions on both mismatch paths and `status_state` on unknown. Zero code-only refusal rows remain outside the two helpers, the bound-child surfacing check, and mismatch checks paired with identity assertions. Matches the sibling leaf's 0/29 → all-asserted shape.\n+- FIX (F21): five foreign-major malformed versions (`3.0`, `3.0.0.0`, `.0.0`, `3..0`, `3.b.c`) asserting `provider_protocol_error`; each of the four deleted `parseMajor` arms now promotes its shape to `incompatible_protocol` and reddens.\n+- FIX (F22): token floor pinned two-sided — 31 decoded bytes refused, 32 accepted. Floors `< 8`, `< 16` killed by the 31-byte row; `< 48` killed by the 32-byte row and the 38-byte valid fixture.\n+- FIX (F23): `readCapped` cap path tested both halves — over-cap cut to exactly cap bytes with prefix content (kills truncation removal), error-past-the-cap never reached (kills limiter removal), under/exact-cap passthrough.\n+- FIX (F24): request side gains the exact-boundary test the response side had — limit+1 refused with arm identity, limit accepted. Halving the request bound reddens.\n+- FIX (F26): `exit 3` / `exit 0` silent plugins driven through production `ExecRunner` + `Host.Call`; the both-sites-cleared exit-code mutant reproduces the reviewer's exact `process_failed` → `protocol_error` flip and is killed.\n+- FIX (F27): stdin capture through production `ExecRunner` asserts frame + one `\\n`; the omitted-terminator mutant reddens.\n+- FIX (F28/F29): orphaned discovery paragraph moved back above the JSONL section; the \"proven by narrowing mutants\" sentence restated to what the tests pin (arm identities, 31/32 token bytes, both exact frame bounds).\n+- FINDING: the crash-exit test as first written was flaky — a plugin that exits without draining stdin races stdin writes into EPIPE, surfacing `runner reported no result` instead of the exit-code path. Fixed by draining stdin in the fixture scripts; the flake is in the fixture, not production.\n+- EQUIVALENT (declared, not chased): M09b — narrowing the `checkResponseMembers` required list to drop `\"ok\"` changes nothing observable, because the missing-`ok` pre-check in `DecodeResponse` fires first on every input missing `ok`. The list entry is unreachable defense in depth. Single-site R17 (clearing only the `ExitError`-branch reassignment) is likewise a no-op because the `Result` literal already carries `ProcessState.ExitCode()`; the behavior-bearing mutant clears both sites and is killed.\n+- EVIDENCE: 19-mutant verify sweep (`/tmp/rev2-verify.sh`, cp-aside/cp-back per mutant, presence asserted, restore byte-verified): 18 killed, 1 declared equivalent (M09b). True two-site R17 verified killed separately with the reviewer's exact flip. `go test ./...` exit 0 (15/15), `-race` on provhost exit 0, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt gate clean, `go build` on linux/windows exit 0, `tracecheck` exit 0 unchanged (17/403, 74 cases). provhost cover 86.1% → 88.1%.\n+- BOUND (stated plainly, widened the wrong way): `provhost` does not import `internal/provider` (only a comment at `runner.go:44`), so this leaf is not the first production caller; `provhost` itself has no production caller and there is no `cmd/ax`. Two orphaned packages, every `Host.Call` assertion made from a test. The non-retryability sentence in `doc.go` is now asserted on every refusal row rather than standing on prose.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n+\n+### 0429 — Provider JSONL host leaf: protocol transport, three inherited findings, one repeated harness failure\n"}}}
