{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d171","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f12-fa6f-76e2-8836-346b2c16c0e2"},"sequence":1811,"recorded_at":1780531400003617,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"442e1aa4-e9ef-4d3f-b619-88e6c26afaec"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Round-2 rework is handed off to review (`to-review`, 15/15 checklist, evidence attached, tree left uncommitted).\n\nWhat changed (all test-only; production untouched, F18/F19/F20 closers undisturbed):\n\n- F25 first: every refusal row now names its arm — `requireFrameRefusal` (code + `member` + rule detail + non-retryable) and `requireLocalRefusal`, plus `observed` on both mismatch paths and `status_state` on unknown. Zero code-only refusal rows remain.\n- F21: five foreign-major malformed versions (`3.0`, `3.0.0.0`, `.0.0`, `3..0`, `3.b.c`); each deleted `parseMajor` arm now promotes to `incompatible_protocol` and reddens.\n- F22: token floor pinned two-sided, 31 bytes refused / 32 accepted.\n- F23: `readCapped` cap path tested both halves (cut-to-cap + stop-consuming via error-past-cap reader).\n- F24: exact-boundary request-side frame test (limit+1 refused, limit framed).\n- F26/F27: exit-3/exit-0 plugins and stdin byte-capture through production `ExecRunner` + `Host.Call`.\n- F28/F29: orphaned README paragraph moved back; narrowing-mutants claim restated to measured pins. LOGBOOK records the widened orphan bound (two callerless packages) plainly.\n\nVerification: 19-mutant sweep with cp-aside restores and byte-verified restores — 18 killed, 2 declared equivalent with proofs (M09b unreachable behind the `ok` pre-check; single-site R17 a no-op, while the true two-site clear reproduces the exact `process_failed`→`protocol_error` flip and is killed). Full suite 15/15 exit 0, `-race`, both vets, gofmt gate, linux/windows builds, and `tracecheck` (unchanged 17/403) all green; provhost coverage 86.1% → 88.1%.\n\nOne finding worth knowing: my first crash-exit fixture was flaky (a no-read `exit 3` script races stdin into EPIPE) — fixed by draining stdin in the fixtures, fixture-side not production-side.","reason":null}}
